ns: weak memory for numbers, pretentious, uncooperative, makes nasty remarks. No mitigation known.\n\nCandidate C: strengths: 100% reliable, excellent attention, makes correct decisions quickly, calm under pressure, creates positive atmosphere, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: weak leadership, hot temper, arrogance, loner.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Reliability and attention are top. C is 100% reliable and excellent attention. B is conscientious but has weak memory for numbers (attention). So C seems stronger on safety-critical criteria. Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe manageable. D has good concentration and problem solving but weak leadership and temperament issues. A has leadership but interpersonal issues and unknown reliability.\n\nThus I think C is best overall. I will vote Candidate C. Provide argument referencing earlier discussion: building on Agent 2's support for C, but also addressing Agent 1's concerns about B's numerical weakness. Emphasize that C's reliability and attention outweigh B's concerns, and that communication can be trained.\n\nNow produce public message and metadata."}
