ing toward C. As Agent 1, we can either maintain B or shift. We need to provide argument.\n\nWe should consider the criteria: reliability, attention, decision quality, stress, communication, crew cooperation. Candidate B's weak memory for numbers is a serious safety issue. Candidate C's communication difficulty is also serious but perhaps trainable. The panel seems to think reliability and attention are paramount. So maybe Agent 1 should reconsider and shift to Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 and 3 argued for C, highlighting B's memory weakness. Agent 1 earlier highlighted B's strengths. Now we can say after hearing concerns, I am less convinced by B's memory weakness and will shift to C.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B has weak memory for numbers; C is 100% reliable, excellent attention, makes correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis. Also note C's communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education, but we consider these manageable.\n\nThus vote for Candidate C.\n\nWe need to output PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
